worrying about vibration or speed.

133
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:52,677
Which means, then...

134
00:09:52,760 --> 00:09:55,584
No one has survived a
direct hit by that attack.

135
00:09:55,860 --> 00:09:56,860
Caesar couldn't.

136
00:09:57,060 --> 00:10:00,500
And now you will taste Divine Sandstorm!

137
00:10:19,580 --> 00:10:22,457
Even if it lasted only the
distance of half a lap,

138
00:10:22,540 --> 00:10:25,720
it was a battle filled with
many twists and surprises.

139
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:27,720
But in the end,

140
00:10:27,840 --> 00:10:32,193
Wamu proved the superiority of both
his thinking and his fighting prowess.

141
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:38,229
I think the next battle is going
to be quite a test of will.

142
00:10:38,960 --> 00:10:41,784
Truly, it is not my
preference to fight a woman.

143
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:44,480
Wamu dislikes it even more.

144
00:10:45,820 --> 00:10:49,460
Notwithstanding, all users of
Hamon must be done away with.

145
00:10:51,860 --> 00:10:52,800
Drink that.

146
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:57,417
It will provide a painless death thanks

147
00:10:57,500 --> 00:11:00,017
that's quite considerate
of you but Jojo seems

148
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:01,917
to be a little less dead than you thought

149
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:05,640
huh Lord course look
out there in the arena

150
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:10,220
It can't be

151
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:14,840
Lord Wamu's arms They look
like they're about to fall off

152
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:20,670
Madness

153
00:11:21,360 --> 00:11:24,240
How could this have
possibly happened to me?

154
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:26,480
What's wrong?

155
00:11:26,740 --> 00:11:32,280
What is happening to Wamu out there?
Look! There! It's Jojo! He's alive!

156
00:11:32,560 --> 00:11:33,500
He's moving!

157
00:11:33,740 --> 00:11:35,200
He's not even hurt!

158
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:41,360
Well, I apparently managed
to survive once again.

159
00:11:41,780 --> 00:11:45,660
But Wamuu hit him directly with
his divine sandstorm attack.

160
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:47,320
How could he?

161
00:11:47,980 --> 00:11:48,810
Directly?

162
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:53,657
Jojo was cunning enough to make
it look like it was a direct hit.

163
00:11:53,740 --> 00:11:57,300
He is an absolute genius at
trickery and misdirection.

164
00:11:57,540 --> 00:12:00,834
But I'm not sure I should be
giving him praise for that.

165
00:12:01,920 --> 00:12:04,500
Take a close look at Wamuu's arms.

166
00:12:07,440 --> 00:12:09,440
Oh, wait, now I see.

167
00:12:12,800 --> 00:12:16,976
He wrapped the reins around Wamuu's
arms after filling them with Hamon.

168
00:12:18,020 --> 00:12:20,820
Wamuu's divine sandstorm
was short-circuited.

169
00:12:21,620 --> 00:12:24,497
Wamuu was already sticking
one hand out of the horse.

170
00:12:24,580 --> 00:12:27,237
He was going to try to
use his divine sandstorm.

171
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:31,277
However, in order to do so, I knew he'd
have to stick his other hand out too.

172
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:34,000
And I had the perfect
counter for that move.

173
00:12:34,620 --> 00:12:36,680
Lord Wamu's face! Look at him!

174
00:12:36,860 --> 00:12:38,720
He's in agony! See that?

175
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:41,037
He doesn't seem to know where he's going!

176
00:12:41,120 --> 00:12:42,296
His eyes are vacant!

177
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:43,520
What should we do?

178
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:45,500
It's the second lap!

179
00:12:45,820 --> 00:12:47,408
But what's going to happen?

180
00:12:47,660 --> 00:12:50,140
Lord Wamu can't hold a weapon like that!

181
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:52,780
Is it even possible for him to fight?

182
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:54,560
It's not a surprise.

183
00:12:55,360 --> 00:12:59,817
Right in mid-attack, Wamu was
struck with a lethal dose of Homo.

184
00:12:59,900 --> 00:13:04,360
The confidence built up over
millennia of triumph has crumbled.

185
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:09,920
The quiet, calm intensity his
victories gave him has vanished.

186
00:13:11,020 --> 00:13:13,380
A tragic shock for him.

187
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:15,940
But it matters not at all.

188
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:18,920
Put out the next set of
weapons and do it now!

189
00:13:22,820 --> 00:13:24,680
Lord Kars has given the order.

190
00:13:24,980 --> 00:13:26,980
When he speaks, we must obey!

191
00:13:31,220 --> 00:13:34,640
For the second lap, both
warriors will receive crossbows.

192
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:37,880
Each comes with ammunition for two shots.

193
00:13:38,340 --> 00:13:42,164
The first warrior there has the
choice of the small or large bow.

194
00:13:54,160 --> 00:13:55,240
What's this now?

195
00:13:55,420 --> 00:13:56,457
There's two weapons.

196
00:13:56,540 --> 00:13:59,305
There's a large one and
another that's smaller.

197
00:14:00,420 --> 00:14:03,837
Lisa, Lisa, this is what's
going through your thoughts now.

198
00:14:03,920 --> 00:14:07,038
Wamuu's mind is in no
condition to entertain a fight.

199
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:11,077
So why then would Kars be
deploying these new weapons,

200
00:14:11,160 --> 00:14:13,160
and with such apparent confidence?

201
00:14:13,620 --> 00:14:15,960
It's very unsettling, is it not?

202
00:14:16,300 --> 00:14:21,660
Well, the reason is that at his core, Wamuu
is a warrior of legendary mental power.

203
00:14:22,260 --> 00:14:26,966
The very best athletes use a psychological
technique called the Switch Comeback.

204
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:31,917
When these champions are brought low by
the pressure of shock, failure, or fear,

205
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,597
they can flip a mental
switch and bring out their

206
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:37,386
fighting spirit for one
last Herculean effort.

207
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:43,180
Desperate times call for desperate
measures, and Whamu will win at any cost!

208
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:46,920
No, I don't believe it!

209
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:49,100
Did he really just do that? What?

210
00:14:49,280 --> 00:14:50,400
No, Lord Whamu!

211
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:52,120
Look, his eyes are gone!

212
00:14:52,420 --> 00:14:54,460
He poked out his eyes!

213
00:14:56,760 --> 00:15:00,320
I foolishly relied on my eyes
because I was able to see,

214
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:02,700
and Jojo exploited my weakness.

215
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:10,200
Now I will use this horn to see things
outlined in wind instead of light.

216
00:15:14,140 --> 00:15:17,760
He flipped the switch by removing
his eyes from the equation.

217
00:15:18,040 --> 00:15:20,864
Now he is once again
psychologically invincible.

218
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:24,780
He senses the wind with
that horn on his forehead.

219
00:15:25,700 --> 00:15:29,140
He sees air better than he did light. Huh?

220
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:30,967
What is that supposed to be?

221
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:33,711
That's not going to have any effect on me.

222
00:15:35,260 --> 00:15:37,613
Because of you, I lost my friend Caesar.

223
00:15:37,860 --> 00:15:39,213
Try any trick you want.

224
00:15:39,300 --> 00:15:42,006
I'll do whatever it takes
to finish the fight.

225
00:15:42,840 --> 00:15:45,040
Jojo, which crossbow will you take?

226
00:15:45,140 --> 00:15:46,081
Yeah, which one?

227
00:15:46,220 --> 00:15:47,220
You need to ask.

228
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:49,047
You know the answer to that.

229
00:15:49,700 --> 00:15:52,160
The large one, you stupid morons.

230
00:15:52,460 --> 00:15:53,820
Power is what I want.

231
00:15:55,520 --> 00:15:58,040
You gotta admit that one does have power.

232
00:15:58,280 --> 00:16:00,020
Yeah, lots of power.

233
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:03,240
Oh, come on!

234
00:16:03,480 --> 00:16:05,320
I can't even draw this thing.

235
00:16:05,860 --> 00:16:09,560
It's so tight, I can't get the
string to go anywhere at all.

236
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:11,910
You like it?

237
00:16:11,993 --> 00:16:13,357
You got greedy, didn't you?

238
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:17,440
Even a normal crossbow takes a huge
amount of strength to draw back.

239
00:16:17,680 --> 00:16:19,621
You had to have the big one, huh?

240
00:16:19,900 --> 00:16:21,540
That's what greed gets you.

241
00:16:27,940 --> 00:16:31,293
I will use the first ball to
paint a picture of the wind.

242
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:43,320
Now that I know what the range
is, the next shot will not miss.

243
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:47,277
How am I supposed to defend myself
if I can't shoot this thing?

244
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:48,980
Lord Wobble, shoot him!

245
00:16:49,180 --> 00:16:50,620
Blow us the smithereens!

246
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:53,700
Let us snack on whatever
small pieces remain.

247
00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:10,320
Right, just as I thought.

248
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:14,637
The wind stirred up by these fires makes
it hard for him to figure out where I am.

249
00:17:14,720 --> 00:17:16,100
